    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85-a4">

                <pb facs="0280" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg210"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 244.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Young to Mr. Seymour.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 27,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your dispatch No. 29, in
                    reference to the disturbances in Canton. The measures taken by you to preserve
                    order were prompt and salutary. It is a pleasure to know that the viceroy was so
                    willing to answer your demands, and also to learn that no Americans were
                    concerned in what seems to have been a wanton and foolish outrage upon Chinese
                    society.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. RUSSELL YOUNG.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
